invariant: INV-39
file: srv_handshake.c
catches: tcp_blocking_loop_test
reason: the tcp-blocking server answers a second ClientHello that has
  bytes after it in its record with a ServerHello. The HelloRetryRequest
  path has a check of its own, so this edit removes that one alone. RFC
  9846 section 5.1 makes those bytes unexpected_message.
  test/tcp_blocking_retry_tests.h adds one byte to the second hello's
  record and requires that alert in the clear after the retry.

--- old
    // The read key changes after the ServerHello, so the second hello
    // must end its record (hsr_check_record_end). The first hello needs
    // no such check: the read key does not change between the two.
    rc = hsr_check_record_end(h);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        return rc;
    }
--- new
